      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__xcert__apis_1gafc17a8e6c3a9c36de72923ddf5ec9a84" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int XCert_GenerateX509Cert</definition>
        <argsstring>(u64 X509CertAddr, u32 MaxCertSize, u32 *X509CertSize, XCert_Config *Cfg)</argsstring>
        <name>XCert_GenerateX509Cert</name>
        <param>
          <type>u64</type>
          <declname>X509CertAddr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>u32</type>
          <declname>MaxCertSize</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>u32 *</type>
          <declname>X509CertSize</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="struct_x_cert___config" kindref="compound">XCert_Config</ref> *</type>
          <declname>Cfg</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function creates the X.509 Certificate/Certificate Signing Request(CSR) </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>X509CertAddr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Address of the X.509 Certificate buffer </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>MaxCertSize</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Maximum size of the X.509 Certificate buffer </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>X509CertSize</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Size of X.509 Certificate in bytes </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Cfg</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to structure which includes configuration for the X.509 Certificate.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS Successfully generated X.509 certificate/CSR</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_INVALID_PARAM Invalid function arguments</para></listitem><listitem><para>XCERT_ERR_X509_KAT_FAILED Failure of SHA384 KAT</para></listitem><listitem><para>XCERT_ERR_X509_GEN_TBSCERT_DIGEST Failure in SHA 384 digest calculation for TBS certificate</para></listitem><listitem><para>XCERT_ERR_X509_GET_SIGN Failure in getting stored signature</para></listitem><listitem><para>XSECURE_KAT_MAJOR_ERROR Failure in Sign Generate KAT</para></listitem><listitem><para>XCERT_ERR_X509_CALC_SIGN Failure in generating ephemeral key and signature</para></listitem><listitem><para>XCERT_ERR_X509_UPDATE_ENCODED_LEN Failure in updating encoded length</para></listitem><listitem><para>XCERT_ERR_X509_INSUFFICIENT_MEMORY Insufficient buffer provided for X.509 cert.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_FAILURE In case of failure</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Certificate ::= SEQUENCE { tbsCertificate TBSCertificate, signatureAlgorithm AlgorithmIdentifier, signatureValue BIT STRING } </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para>SHA 384 is used to calculate hash for Serial field and to calculate hash for signature calculation. So run KAT for SHA384 before use</para><para>Generate Sign Algorithm field</para><para>Calculate SHA 384 Digest of the TBS certificate</para><para>Get the TBS certificate signature stored in Cert DB</para><para>If the Signature is available, compare the hash stored with the hash calculated to make sure nothing is changed. if hash matches, copy the stored signature else generate the signature again.</para><para>If the Signature is not available or Hash comparison from above fails, regenerate the signature.</para><para>Calculate signature of the TBS certificate using the private key</para><para>Copy the generated signature and hash into SignStore</para><para>Generate Signature field</para><para>Update the encoded length in the X.509 certificate SEQUENCE</para><para>Validate the certificate size and copy the certificate to user buffer</para>        </inbodydescription>
